events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/pulls/68704","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68704","diff_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68704.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/68704.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds source-grounded design invariants to `src/Components/AGENTS.md`, with legitimate exceptions documented alongside each rule so the guidance does not create false review findings.\n\nThe guidance covers:\n\n- render-mode agnosticism and the narrow render-mode-specific assembly exceptions\n- `HttpContext` access and cross-render-mode service registration\n- `StateHasChanged`, `InvokeAsync`, and `IHandleEvent` behavior\n- trimming/AOT annotations and dependency expectations\n- deterministic async test coordination\n- Selenium as the Components E2E framework versus Playwright MCP for manual validation\n\nEach rule was checked against the current source tree before inclusion. Stale, withdrawn, out-of-repo, or unverifiable claims from #66964 were deliberately excluded. The original maintainer review that motivated this grounding pass is [Javier's review on #66964](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/66964#pullrequestreview-4436642622).\n\n## Validation\n\n- Verified every cited source path and reference pattern exists in the current tree\n- Confirmed `IHttpContextAccessor` has no shipping Components source usages\n- Grounded `StateHasChanged` guidance in analyzer BL0012 and its explicit lambda/local-function exclusions\n- Confirmed the Components E2E project references Selenium and not Playwright\n- Confirmed the current `src/Components/AGENTS.md` blob on upstream `main` was unchanged before applying the edit\n- `git diff --check`\n\nDocumentation only; no runtime behavior changes.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68704/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/68704/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/67176","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/67176/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/67176/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/67176/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/67176","id":4647697426,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAQzde87lrQxw","number":67176,"title":"Adding StateHasChanged analyzer to flag unnecessary calls.","user":{"login":"MayaKirova","id":10397980,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzk3OTgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10397980?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova","html_url":"https://github.com/MayaKirova","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MayaKirova/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"p